{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789859827,"nonce":"DHjc1faDm+rFz8hs9FqrJGiBfx4=","title":"A Python program with no top-level statement has no entry, so the whole library is built up front","message":"The frontend emits __main__ only when the module body has statements. A file of only defs, or an empty one, has no function named by the entry point, initial_wanted returns None, and every one of the library's 617 functions is optimised and compiled before anything runs: `zypy run empty.py` took 192 ms of wall (compile 174) against 20 ms for `print(1)`, PyPy 19, CPython 16.\n\nThe module body is now always the entry, empty or not: 9.6 ms of compile.","files":null}]}